# Navigating the ia-dev-workflow Skill

The skill lives at `~/.cursor/skills/ia-dev-workflow/` and has exactly three layers.
Do NOT read all three files end-to-end — route by need:

| Layer | File | Read it when |
|---|---|---|
| Decision layer | `SKILL.md` | Always start here. Steps 1–9 = workflow order; each step links to detail sections. |
| Command layer | `reference.md` | You know WHAT to do and need the exact command/API payload. |
| Diagnosis layer | `troubleshooting.md` | Something failed and you need signature → cause → fix. |

## Routing table (symptom/need → exact section)

- Environment setup / server / ngrok / stack: `SKILL.md` Step 1 → `reference.md` §1
  (§1.3 = scripted health check + stack-drift detection)
- Run a flow, poll jobs, per-bubble results, retry errors: Step 2 → `reference.md` §2.1–2.2
- Change settings (persistSettings), platform scripts, locked fields/reinstall: Step 3 →
  `reference.md` §2.3–2.5
- Inspect NetSuite/Shopify records, SuiteQL, saved searches: Step 4 → `reference.md` §3
- Data disappears between bubbles / timeouts / "random" duplicates: Step 5 →
  `troubleshooting.md` (debug logs, governance, rerun probe)
- SuiteScript / bundle rebuild + deploy: Step 6 → `reference.md` §4
- End-to-end verification harness + sandbox cleanup: Step 7 →
  `troubleshooting.md` § Cleanup checklist
- Fresh tile install (license, TBA, DIY Shopify token): Step 8 → `reference.md` §2.7
- First order won't sync on a fresh tile: Step 9 → `reference.md` §2.8
- Unknown error message: grep `troubleshooting.md` § "Failure signature → cause" for the
  literal error text FIRST, before diagnosing from scratch.

## Search technique

Use targeted lookup, not full reads: `rg -in '<error text or keyword>'
~/.cursor/skills/ia-dev-workflow/` and then read only the matching section. Section
anchors in SKILL.md links (e.g. `reference.md#28-...`) are stable — follow them directly.
